            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For reference, I did go with setting [informative statusline](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a5ea026f6b997399a2899559bd7381d8fb67dd4/scripts/minimal_init.lua#L10). Having information about file name is rarely useful (but sometimes it is), but information about current line and column (both byte and virtual) is useful. This resulted in to [*a lot* of changed screenshots](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/3a5ea026f6b997399a2899559bd7381d8fb67dd4), though.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">For reference, I did go with setting <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a5ea026f6b997399a2899559bd7381d8fb67dd4/scripts/minimal_init.lua#L10\">informative statusline</a>. Having information about file name is rarely useful (but sometimes it is), but information about current line and column (both byte and virtual) is useful. This resulted in to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/3a5ea026f6b997399a2899559bd7381d8fb67dd4\"><em>a lot</em> of changed screenshots</a>, though.</p>",
            "bodyText": "For reference, I did go with setting informative statusline. Having information about file name is rarely useful (but sometimes it is), but information about current line and column (both byte and virtual) is useful. This resulted in to a lot of changed screenshots, though.",
